The file dialog belongs to the desktop
====================================

"Choose my model folder" was calling `pick_folder`, which reached for `kdialog` — a KDE utility that is
not the file manager and is not installed on most systems. On a box without it the button did nothing
at all, which reads as a broken app rather than a missing tool. The multi-select pickers in the same
file had already been going through the XDG desktop portal, which is the dialog the session itself
uses; the single-pick pair just never got the same treatment.

Both of them go through `org.freedesktop.portal.FileChooser` now, with `directory: true` for folders,
and fall back to kdialog/zenity only if no portal answers. Verified on this machine: the portal returns
a request handle, `xdg-desktop-portal-kde` draws the dialog, and what appears is the KDE chooser — Places
sidebar, breadcrumbs, the same one Dolphin opens — not something the app drew itself.

**The memory palace default moved to Documents.** `~/memory-palace` was the right instinct and the
wrong folder: on Linux the desktop decides where Documents is, through
`~/.config/user-dirs.dirs`, and it can be localised or moved to another mount. `paths::documents_dir()`
reads that file now (`XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR`, `$HOME` expanded, falling back to `~/Documents`) and the
palace defaults to `Documents/memory-palace` — a folder that shows up in the person's file manager
without them having to hunt for it.

Preference order is unchanged: the folder chosen at setup, then `QUIXI_PALACE_DIR`, then this default.

